* German Trio (3-channel 100 W German head: Clean / Crunch / Lead) preamp, stage 1 of 5: the guitar, V1A (shared by the three channels)
* and the input networks of the channels up to the wiper of each gain pot. Transcribed from the service manual drawing.
*
* The relays that pick the channel (contacts CL, CR, LE) are the SW_ resistors, set by the "channel" selector in amp.json.
* Clean: CL -> EQ (MID 100k, the 10n/10k network, HIGH 1M, LOW 1M, 220p, 100k, 22n x2) -> GAIN CLEAN 1M (with the BRIGHT 100p) -> V1B (stage 2).
* Crunch and Lead: 562k || 2.2n, the contact, then the gain pot. Crunch has 150k and 82k5 in front of its 100k pot and a 1n bright cap from
* the pot's input to its wiper; Lead drives its 250k pot directly with a 1n bright cap. Both feed V2A (stage 3) from the wiper (node g2).
* The two pots are one element here (VRG: 100k for Crunch, 250k for Lead, changed by the selector) because the plug-in has one set of knobs
* for both channels.
*
* The V1 rail is a fixed source at the value that gives the 185 V the drawing shows on V1A's plate.
* Units: k M, m u n p. Node "0" is ground. See engine/include/sas/netlist.h for the format.

V VRAIL x 100 380
V VX1 x1 50 357
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
* The guitar behind its source impedance (see the other amps): coil, winding capacitance, loss, cable.
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p

* V1A: grid straight on the jack with a 1M leak, 221k plate load, 1k82 + 1u cathode, 47n coupling, 1M at the coupling's output.
R R1M in 0 1M
T V1A in p1a k1a 12AX7
R R221 x1 p1a 221k
R RK1 k1a 0 1k82
C CK1 k1a 0 1u
C C47 p1a p1 47n
R R1MP1 p1 0 1M

* Clean channel: contact CL, then the EQ.
R SW_CL p1 n0 1
C CC10a n0 fi 10n
R RC10k fi 0 10k
C CC10b fi pm 10n
R VRCM_T n0 tn 1
R VRCM_B tn pm 1
C CC220 tn hl 220p
R RC100 tn dd 100k
R VRCH_T hl hw 1
R VRCH_B hw hb 1
C CC22a hb dd 22n
R VRCL hb mm 1
C CC22b mm dd 22n
R RC10b mm 0 10k
* GAIN CLEAN 1M and the BRIGHT switch (100p from the pot's top to its wiper).
R VRGC_T hw gw 1
R VRGC_B gw 0 1
C CBR hw bs 100p
R SW_BRIGHT bs gw 1e12

* Crunch: 562k || 2.2n, contact CR, 150k and 82k5 into the gain pot, 1n bright cap to the wiper.
R R562c p1 x1c 562k
C C22c p1 x1c 2.2n
R SW_CR x1c xc 1e12
R R150 xc jc 150k
R R82k5 jc 0 82.5k
R SW_JC jc gj 1e12
C CB1c xc g2 1n
* Lead: the same 562k || 2.2n and contact LE, straight onto the pot, 1n bright cap.
R R562l p1 x1l 562k
C C22l p1 x1l 2.2n
R SW_LE x1l xl 1e12
R SW_JL xl gj 1e12
C CB1l xl g2 1n
* The shared gain pot and V2A's grid leak.
R VRG_T gj g2 1
R VRG_B g2 0 1
R R1MG2 g2 0 1M
